Create a go program with a proper structure under a new directory called backend, which when launched should have one set of periodic tasks, one set of stateless http handlers and http server called portal-api, another set of stateless http handlers and a http server called mesh-api, and, one mcp server. 

The golang program should have a Config struct which should be set via env variables when the program launches. The two env variable that must be there, in addition to the others as needed from below requirements, would be an "ENV" for the environment which could have values "dev", "ci", "staging", "prod" as possible values; And another "TENANT_ID" which could have values "sgp", "usa1", "deu", "ind1".

There should be structured logging via slog. 

The program needs to connect to a postgres database using the pgx driver. The connection parameters should come from env.

There should be a directory called migrations in the top-level directory. Under this directory, there should be a directory called "common", and other directories for each of the above mentioned tenants.  Two tables hub_users and orgs should be created on the .sql file under common. Use pressly/goose for database migrations from golang. The per-tenant migration SQL files should have seed data to create test users.

There should be three top-level directories called orgs-ui, hub-ui and admin-ui each of which should have a Dockerfile that should just serve some static HTML content, saying the portal name.

Create a docker-compose-dev file which should bring up the above tenants, with each tenant having an traefik server as the entrypoint, an API server from the Golang sources, a postgresql database, and the three portals. The "common" migrations should be a docker image. The per-tenant migrations should be run via psql. 

